From 7cb22f632f82ed1ac9f4e95abd3422c6ce52c5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:15:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim): f32 twin of the cell cut kernel and the brick
 work list

GPU stock sim S1. A CPU f32 twin of the per-cell cut kernel, on
tile-relative coordinates (tile = brick), with a claim margin so that
the twin never removes more than the f64 field cut. The max law runs
on order-preserving u32 keys (the GPU atomicMax law). The brick work
list uses the f64 sweep windows, clipped to the pack_cut lattice and
sorted brick-major. Only the upright ball and flat end mill on linear
moves have a twin; other tools, arcs, tilted axes, zero-length and
non-finite moves refuse by name. No caller changes.

Pinned by crates/sim/tests/stock_cut_twin.rs (7 tests).

Fixes #2626

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
